      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the fundamental question for this change is that whether `commitGraph. changedPathsVersion` requires us to keep commit graph data in memory consistent with the flag. Under this change, we are always reading the BF into memory, then choose to serve/hide it based on the flag value.  \n\nWe should check whether there\u0027s other ways of logging the commit graph data (or its related metadata) from the cache outside of the `getCommitGraph` code path. We need to be absolutely sure `getCommitGraph` gate keeps all potential callers. \n\nThough I think that the absolute error proof option is to keep the in-memory CG consistent with the flag value; \n\ni.e. boolean hasCpfData \u003d (getChangedPathFilter(0) !\u003d null);\nif (hasCpfData !\u003d flag) {\n    // reload from the commitGraphLoader.\n}",
